# Environment Variables Template

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values.
**Never commit `.env` to version control.**

```bash
# ============================================================
# Instana Connection
# ============================================================

# Base URL of your Instana unit. Format: https://<unit>.instana.io
# Required. No trailing slash.
#
# React/Vite app:
VITE_INSTANA_BASE_URL=https://myunit.instana.io
# Node.js scripts:
INSTANA_BASE_URL=https://myunit.instana.io

# API token with at least read access to Application Monitoring.
# Generate in: Instana UI → Settings → API Tokens → Add API Token
# Required. Treat this as a password — never commit it.
#
# ⚠️  Vite embeds VITE_* vars into the browser bundle at build time.
#     For production, use a backend proxy instead of exposing the token
#     in the React app.
#
# React/Vite app:
VITE_INSTANA_API_TOKEN=
# Node.js scripts:
INSTANA_API_TOKEN=

# ============================================================
# Optional — Client Behaviour
# ============================================================

# HTTP timeout in milliseconds.
# Default: 30000 (30 seconds)
# VITE_INSTANA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# INSTANA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Maximum number of retry attempts for transient 5xx errors.
# Default: 3
# VITE_INSTANA_MAX_RETRIES=3
# INSTANA_MAX_RETRIES=3

# ============================================================
# Optional — React Query (dashboard)
# ============================================================

# staleTime in ms for application/service lists (stable data).
# Default: 60000 (60 seconds)
# VITE_INSTANA_STABLE_STALE_TIME=60000

# refetchInterval in ms for live panels (traces, KPIs).
# Default: 30000 (30 seconds)
# VITE_INSTANA_REFETCH_INTERVAL=30000

# ============================================================
# Optional — Vite Dev Server
# ============================================================

# Port for the Vite development server.
# Default: 5173
# VITE_PORT=5173
```

---

## Security Reminders

1. Add `.env` to `.gitignore` immediately after creating it.
2. Use a **read-only** API token for monitoring integrations — never an admin token.
3. Rotate the token if it is ever accidentally exposed (committed to git, logged, etc.).
4. In CI/CD, inject `INSTANA_API_TOKEN` as a masked secret.
5. For production React apps, **do not** embed the token in the Vite bundle. Route API calls through a backend proxy (e.g. a Vite proxy config or an Express middleware) that injects the token server-side.
